From 580b5554a2c30b88e6a917623f01e4ea5d6b01d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:38:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/32] ehci: never chain an isochronous transfer into frames
 already passed

A transfer queued on an isochronous pipe starts right after the frames of
the pipe's previous one. When the previous transfer had finished and its
successor came late, that anchor was behind the controller: the first
descriptors were linked into frames it had left. They stayed active, the
finisher, which only looks five frames back, did not see them, and a whole
frame list (128 ms) later the controller ran them, into the buffer of a
transfer finished long before. A UVC camera on a Toshiba AC100 lost about
a third of its microphone transactions this way and got pieces of old data
in its video frames.

An anchor that is not ahead of the controller by the margin a new transfer
gets is dropped, and the transfer starts after that margin.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
index 3de6979ac0..0ea8e31b32 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
@@ -2108,6 +2108,22 @@ EHCI::SubmitIsochronous(Transfer *transfer)
 		// Chain off THIS pipe's previous transfer, not a controller-global
 		// anchor: see the iso_anchor comment in the header.
 		int32 anchor = GetIsoAnchor(pipe);
+		if (anchor != -1 && fFirstIsochronousTransfer != NULL) {
+			// The anchor must still be ahead of the controller, with the
+			// margin a new transfer gets. A transfer queued after its
+			// predecessor's last frame had passed was linked into frames
+			// the controller had left: its first descriptors stayed active,
+			// were not seen by the finisher, which only looks a few frames
+			// back, and ran a whole frame list later into the buffer of a
+			// transfer that was long finished.
+			uint32 now = (ReadOpReg(EHCI_FRINDEX) / 8)
+				& (EHCI_VFRAMELIST_ENTRIES_COUNT - 1);
+			uint32 ahead = ((uint32)anchor - now)
+				& (EHCI_VFRAMELIST_ENTRIES_COUNT - 1);
+			uint32 margin = (fThreshold + 7) / 8 + 1;
+			if (ahead < margin || ahead >= EHCI_VFRAMELIST_ENTRIES_COUNT / 2)
+				anchor = -1;
+		}
 		if (fFirstIsochronousTransfer != NULL && anchor != -1)
 			currentFrame = anchor;
 		else {
